portable-pty loads ConPTY from kernel32, then prefers a `conpty.dll` found through the DLL search path, so any
library of that name on PATH or in the working directory is loaded into the process. Only kernel32's exports are used
here, looked up with GetModuleHandleW/GetProcAddress (kernel32 is always loaded), and the `shared_library` dependency
goes.

From herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr, Apache-2.0) vendor/patches/portable-pty/0001-control-conpty-loading.patch,
modified: herdr also loads a hash-checked app-local conpty.dll bundle; ngterm ships none, so only the kernel32 path
is kept. herdr issues #761 and #1533; upstream discussion https://github.com/microsoft/terminal/issues/17452.
Remove when portable-pty stops probing a bare conpty.dll.

